{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T10:20:32.471Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4b084a2f74dd44054f4b141a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1664","lineage:pm-gh1664","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1664","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1664","lineage:pm-gh1664","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1730"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1730: the MCP flat-parameter parity spec compares the output-size token estimate of two concurrent reads that both write the context-usage ledger, so a Windows shard fails when one read waits on the ledger"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1730 (Nightly Validation, windows-latest / Node 24 shard 3/4, run 43589248357 on fcdd5f89d). tests/unit/mcp/read-tool-flat-parameters.spec.ts › 'applies flat intent and limit arguments exactly like nested options' runs the flat and the nested pm_next read concurrently (Promise.all) on one tracker and compared their whole context_intent blocks, which include estimated_tokens (325 vs 313 on the failing shard). Both context and next record context-usage serving rows under the ledger lock (recordContextUsageServing in src/sdk/query/next.ts and context.ts), so the rendered output of two concurrent reads can differ in runtime state (lock wait and signal-store warnings) while their parameter resolution is identical. estimated_tokens measures the rendered output, not the parameters. Root-cause comment already on the issue; family owner pm-2zjs0g is closed. Duplicate check: searched GH-1730, flat parameters, estimated_tokens concurrent reads; no open item owns the spec."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["flaky-test","gh:1730","mcp","nightly","test-reliability","windows"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-20T10:20:32.471Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T10:20:32.471Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":30},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The spec compares every parameter-derived context_intent field of the flat and nested reads and only requires estimated_tokens to be a number on both; it passes regardless of which concurrent read waits on the context-usage ledger"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Flat and nested MCP read arguments are proven to resolve the same intent without depending on concurrent ledger timing"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"A Windows nightly shard failed because two concurrent reads rendered outputs of different sizes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-2zjs0g","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-20T10:20:32.471Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"7d77802eb32fb7d74b597eb84ec39551228c48497ab96ce03deaf74473f0250e","item_hash_